 write('provenance.html','How to use this course','''<p class="eyebrow">A COURSE BUILT AROUND UNDERSTANDING</p><h1>Read, trace, build, explain.</h1><section class="prose"><h2>What changed</h2><p>Chapters now follow explicit dependencies from intermediate foundations to advanced systems. Each has a specific use case, plain definitions, its own interactive flow, explained lessons, code, and a practical experiment. Topic coverage determines chapter depth; no fixed number of questions is required.</p><h2>Two reading depths</h2><p>Start with the guided explanations and concrete cases. Use the additional interview questions for technical depth, trade-offs, and failure boundaries. Existing question identifiers are preserved even though their chapters moved. New guided lessons have independent stable identifiers.</p><h2>Scope and evidence</h2><p>The platform and data are fictional. This website does not expose private project code or call model providers. Standard-library examples use synthetic fixtures. Optional agent SDK examples are syntax-checked sketches; the OCR engine and SQL fragments are not executed. The synthetic FastAPI lab has authentication, ownership, SSE replay, cancellation, and WebSocket checks, but uses process-local state.</p><h2>Your study record</h2><p>Notes and learned flags are personal study tools, not certification. They stay in your browser and can be exported. No print control is included; core content remains readable without JavaScript. Interactive examples are deterministic teaching simulations, not live model output.</p></section>''')
